Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There is no option in the gheatmap man page to change the cell border width (I am using v 1.8.2). If anyone else is having this problem, I did discover that setting color = NA removes the cell border. Having an option to specify the width might be a nice addition for the future.

On Mon, Oct 9, 2017 at 12:05 AM Yu, Guangchuang <gc...@connect.hku.hk> wrote:

> please refer to the function man page:
> ?gheatmap
> ​
>
> On Tue, Oct 3, 2017 at 10:07 PM, Tatum Mortimer <tatumdm...@gmail.com> wrote:
> > Is it possible to change the width of the cell border in gheatmap? I have a large tree (~800 tips), which causes the cell border to take up the majority or all of the cell when I plot my data matrix.
> >
> > --
